DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The cchhrroooott command changes its root directory to the supplied directory
     _n_e_w_r_o_o_t and executes _c_o_m_m_a_n_d, if supplied, or an interactive copy of the
     user's shell.

     The cchhrroooott command is restricted to the superuser.

     The options are as follows:

     --gg _g_r_o_u_p[,_g_r_o_u_p[,_._._.]]
             Override the primary and supplemental group IDs.  The primary
             group ID is set to the first group in the list.  Any remaining
             groups are placed in the supplemental group ID vector.  Each
             group listed must exist in the group(5) databases.

     --uu _u_s_e_r
             Set user ID to _u_s_e_r (which must exist in the passwd(5) database).
             The primary and supplemental group IDs will be set based on the
             user's entries in the passwd(5) and group(5) databases unless
             overridden by the --gg option.  Additional settings may be applied
             as specified in login.conf(5) depending on _u_s_e_r's login class.

